UN R26.how_it_applies:
UN R26 applies to the external projections of M1 vehicles. The front bumper module forms part of the vehicle's 'external surface' (§2.3) and falls under the defined terms 'Bumper' (§2.11) and 'Bumper cover' (§2.12). Approval is granted to the vehicle type, not the bumper alone, but the bumper supplier must design the module to comply. This means:
- the general radius and projection rules of §5 for every exposed part above the floor line;
- §6.5 (bumpers);
- §6.3 (grille slats and gap dimensions);
- §6.15 (registration plate bracket);
- §6.1 (ornaments, if a badge or ornament is fitted);
- §6.9 (body-panel folds);
- §6.8 (sheet-metal edges, if a metal stiffener or beam edge is exposed);
- §6.12 (air intake/outlet flaps, if active flaps are fitted);
- §6.17 (aerials, for the keyless-entry aerial).
The measurement methods of Annex 3 (§2.8, §2.9 and the gap method) apply. The towing device cover is an ordinary external-surface part; only the towing ball itself is excluded from scope. Lamp housings (decorative and side signalling), sensor faces and radomes, and the EV charging flap are part of the external surface and are covered by §5. Conformity of production (§8) applies to series parts.
